[DOCUMENT]
TITLE: Training Parser - High-Level Requirements
UID: HLR-DOC
VERSION: 1.0

[GRAMMAR]
ELEMENTS:
- TAG: REQUIREMENT
  FIELDS:
  - TITLE: UID
    TYPE: String
    REQUIRED: True
  - TITLE: TITLE
    TYPE: String
    REQUIRED: True
  - TITLE: STATEMENT
    TYPE: String
    REQUIRED: True
  - TITLE: RATIONALE
    TYPE: String
    REQUIRED: False
  - TITLE: PRIORITY
    TYPE: String
    REQUIRED: False
  RELATIONS:
  - TYPE: Parent

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: HLR-001
TITLE: ANTLR Grammar Parsing
STATEMENT: The system shall parse training data using ANTLR-based grammars.
RATIONALE: ANTLR provides robust grammar-based parsing with support for complex language structures.
PRIORITY: High

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: HLR-002
TITLE: Multiple Input Formats
STATEMENT: The system shall support parsing multiple input data formats (JSON, CSV, text).
RATIONALE: Flexibility in input formats enables integration with various data sources.
PRIORITY: High

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: HLR-003
TITLE: Data Validation
STATEMENT: The system shall validate parsed data against defined schemas.
RATIONALE: Schema validation ensures data integrity and consistency.
PRIORITY: High

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: HLR-004
TITLE: Error Handling
STATEMENT: The system shall provide detailed error messages for malformed input.
RATIONALE: Clear error reporting improves user experience and debugging.
PRIORITY: Medium

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: HLR-005
TITLE: Type Safety
STATEMENT: The system shall enforce strict type checking throughout the codebase.
RATIONALE: Static type checking prevents runtime errors and improves code maintainability.
PRIORITY: Medium

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: HLR-006
TITLE: Documentation Generation
STATEMENT: The system shall support generation of structured documentation from parsed data.
RATIONALE: Auto-generated documentation ensures consistency and reduces manual effort.
PRIORITY: Medium

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: HLR-007
TITLE: Configurable Synonym Loading
STATEMENT: The system shall allow users to configure exercise name synonyms via external configuration files, enabling customization of name mappings without modifying source code.
RATIONALE: External configuration decouples synonym data from application logic, allowing non-developers to maintain and extend name mappings independently.
PRIORITY: High

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: HLR-008
TITLE: Multiple Synonym Configuration Formats
STATEMENT: The system shall support YAML and JSON file formats for synonym configuration files.
RATIONALE: Supporting industry-standard formats (YAML for readability, JSON for programmatic generation) gives users flexibility in tooling and workflow integration.
PRIORITY: Medium

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: HLR-009
TITLE: Synonym Configuration Validation
STATEMENT: The system shall validate synonym configuration files at load time and report descriptive errors for any structural or semantic violations.
RATIONALE: Fail-fast validation at initialization prevents silent misconfiguration and provides actionable feedback to users when configurations are malformed.
PRIORITY: High

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: HLR-010
TITLE: Backward-Compatible Default Synonyms
STATEMENT: The system shall provide built-in default synonym mappings and operate fully without any user-supplied configuration file.
RATIONALE: Backward compatibility ensures existing integrations and users are unaffected by the introduction of external configuration support.
PRIORITY: High

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: HLR-011
TITLE: Synonym-Based Internationalization
STATEMENT: The system shall support internationalization of exercise names by allowing language-specific synonym configuration files to be provided independently per use case.
RATIONALE: Internationalization through configurable synonyms enables adoption across different linguistic communities without requiring code-level changes.
PRIORITY: Medium
